## =============================================================================
## FILING LADDER — ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
## =============================================================================
##
## This file is committed. `just install` copies it to `.env` (gitignored) on
## first run; every command loads `.env` automatically.
##
## Only set the keys for the rungs you intend to run. No key is required to
## materialize a filing into its representations or to count tokens.
## =============================================================================

# SEC EDGAR fair-access requires a User-Agent that identifies you with contact
# info, or EDGAR answers "Undeclared Automated Tool" / HTTP 429. Required for
# filing acquisition (every rung) and the companyfacts rung.
SEC_GOV_USER_AGENT=Your Name your@email.com

# Frontier run — Anthropic direct. The only route with batch pricing and
# citations on the PDF and text rungs.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Second frontier family — OpenAI direct (chat completions). PDF as a file part,
# automatic prompt caching; pass --context-window for the model's window.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Shakedown — NVIDIA Build free tier (OpenAI-compatible). Proves the harness and
# reads the per-rung token ratio; never a published rung. No PDF input, no
# prompt caching, reasoning models need a large max_tokens.
# NVIDIA_BUILD_API_KEY=

# Open-weight column, and any other model — OpenRouter, provider pinned. PDF
# where the host accepts it; the credits charged are recorded on every turn.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Graph rungs 7a/7b — the RoboSystems `sec` graph over MCP (Streamable HTTP,
# X-API-Key). Any key with a subscription to the shared `sec` repository works.
# ROBOSYSTEMS_API_KEY=
ROBOSYSTEMS_API_URL=https://api.robosystems.ai
ROBOSYSTEMS_GRAPH_ID=sec

# Where materialized filings and run outputs land. Defaults to ./data and ./results.
# FILING_LADDER_DATA_DIR=./data
# FILING_LADDER_RESULTS_DIR=./results

# PDF rendering for rung 1 (headless Chrome). Auto-detected on macOS; set if
# Chrome lives elsewhere.
# CHROME_PATH=/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome
